First of all: I'm playing Nethack for about a month now, so I guess I
could be considered a newbie. I don't mind being spoiled at all, as I
find the game hard enough as it is.


After my last human Valkyrie died to a minotaur in Sokoban, my current
one (started on Friday the 13th - hah!) is my first character to
complete both Sokoban and the Gnomish Mines.

On my way up from the Mines, I discovered my first trap of polymorph
ever. I didn't step into it, but I was curious to see if my cat did. So
I lingered around for a while, and yes, it did. And turned into a violet
fungus. I figured that it would be pretty much useless for me like that,
so I waited for an eternity before it finally stepped on the trap a
second time. It became a hill orc, and after deliberately stepping on it
again, a long worm.

Boy, are these things scary. Just thinking of that giant tail gives me
the creeps. It honestly does! My pet, though leashed, now only moved
further away from the trap, but I guess a leash doesn't make a
difference anymore when your pet is much stronger than you are, does it?
I couldn't get it to move even close to the polytrap now, and besides,
it was getting entangled in its own tail all the time.

At a loss what to do, I checked my inventory and found that I had a yet
unidentified wand with me. I quickly tried engraving with it. Turned out
to be a wand of polymorph... so I decided to zap my pet once. And the
result was a purple worm.


After going back to my stash, I am now standing alongside a pet purple
worm which is ten levels higher than me, has twice as much HP as I do,
and swallows everything that dares move into its vicinity. And I can't
yet decide whether that's a good thing (it basically being a killing
machine right now) or a bad thing (I rarely get any corpses this way,
and I have the feeling this might become critical).

Any suggestions what I should do with my new pet? Should I keep it? Or
try polymorphing it again, with possibly unhelpful results?

Another, unrelated question I'd like to ask: My stash now has a total of
15 unidentified spellbooks. Is there any spellbook that might be of any
use to a Valkyrie at all? My intelligence is currently at 7, which makes
me doubt that.


Thanks for reading this far,
- Marcel


